  "reason": "The study reports a systematic review of outcomes measured in mouse models of type 2 diabetes and compares them to outcomes in human clinical trials. However, it does not report a quantitative measure of agreement (e.g., concordance rate, PPV, sensitivity/specificity) between animal and human results. It only states that 21% of pre-clinical outcomes were also measured in clinical trials, which is a measure of overlap, not agreement in results or effect sizes."
